### list_toolbar_threads
List Vercel toolbar comment threads for a team. Returns unresolved threads by default. Use this to see feedback, comments, or discussions on deployments and previews.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `teamId` | string | yes |  | The team ID to get the deployment events for. Alternatively the team slug can be used.<br>Team IDs start with "team_".<br>If you do not know the team ID or slug, it can be found through these mechanism:<br>- Read the file .vercel/project.json if it exists and extract the orgId<br>- Use the `list_teams` tool |
| `projectId` | string | no |  | Filter by project ID |
| `branch` | string | no |  | Filter by branch name |
| `status` | enum | no |  | Filter by status. Defaults to unresolved. Allowed: `resolved`, `unresolved` |
| `page` | string | no |  | Filter by page path (e.g. /docs) or glob (e.g. /docs*) |
| `search` | string | no |  | Search text in comments |
| `limit` | number | no |  | Maximum number of results to return. Defaults to 20. |
| `offset` | number | no |  | Pagination offset |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "vercel", toolName: "list_toolbar_threads", arguments: {"teamId": "team_xxx"} })

